silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_04_negative_witnesses_concrete_anchor_5#geometricgapforrefusedshortcut a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.01_orientation.chapters.15_witness_traceability.sections.04_negative_witnesses.concrete_anchor_5#geometricgapforrefusedshortcut" .
silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_04_negative_witnesses_concrete_anchor_5#geometricgapforrefusedshortcut silm:hasLongDescription "The GeometricGapForRefusedShortcut is The empty cells in the lower row between NegativeWitness_lower and the target column carry the geometric distance the not-exists direct arrow must visibly cross. For the catus-collision case, these cells record that the shortcut bypasses BOTH the type step (no olog sort assignment) AND the gate_refuse step (no admission predicate fired). The visual reach of the arrow from row 2 up to EmptyHomSet is what makes the negative-regression visibly refused. Removing the gap would collapse the shortcut into a short side-arrow and lose its semantic content." .
